{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function createRateLimitedSignal<TValue, TSelected>(\n   value,\n   initialOptions,\n   selector?): [Accessor<TValue>, Setter<TValue>, SolidRateLimiter<Setter<TValue>, TSelected>];","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/solid-pacer/src/rate-limiter/createRateLimitedSignal.ts#L97","children":[{"type":"text","value":"rate-limiter/createRateLimitedSignal.ts:97"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A Solid hook that creates a rate-limited state value that enforces a hard limit on state updates within a time window.\nThis hook combines Solid's createSignal with rate limiting functionality to provide controlled state updates."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rate limiting is a simple \"hard limit\" approach - it allows all updates until the limit is reached, then blocks\nsubsequent updates until the window resets. Unlike throttling or debouncing, it does not attempt to space out\nor intelligently collapse updates. This can lead to bursts of rapid updates followed by periods of no updates."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The rate limiter supports two types of windows:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"'fixed': A strict window that resets after the window period. All updates within the window count\ntowards the limit, and the window resets completely after the period."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"'sliding': A rolling window that allows updates as old ones expire. This provides a more\nconsistent rate of updates over time."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For smoother update patterns, consider:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"createThrottledSignal: When you want consistent spacing between updates (e.g. UI changes)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"createDebouncedSignal: When you want to collapse rapid updates into a single update (e.g. search input)"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rate limiting should primarily be used when you need to enforce strict limits, like API rate limits."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The hook returns a tuple containing:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The rate-limited state value accessor"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A rate-limited setter function that respects the configured limits"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The rateLimiter instance for additional control"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For more direct control over rate limiting without state management,\nconsider using the lower-level createRateLimiter hook instead."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"state-management-and-selector","children":[{"type":"text","value":"State Management and Selector"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The hook uses TanStack Store for reactive state management via the underlying rate limiter instance.\nThe "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"selector"},{"type":"text","value":" parameter allows you to specify which rate limiter state changes will trigger reactive updates,\noptimizing performance by preventing unnecessary subscriptions when irrelevant state changes occur."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default, there will be no reactive state subscriptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and you must opt-in to state\ntracking by providing a selector function. This prevents unnecessary reactive updates and gives you\nfull control over when your component subscribes to state changes. Only when you provide a selector will\nthe reactive system track the selected state values."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Available rate limiter state properties:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"executionCount"},{"type":"text","value":": Number of function executions"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"executionTimes"},{"type":"text","value":": Timestamps of executions tracked for the current window"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maybeExecuteCount"},{"type":"text","value":": Number of calls to maybeExecute"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rejectionCount"},{"type":"text","value":": Number of calls rejected by the rate limit"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isExceeded"},{"type":"text","value":": Whether the rate limit has been reached"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"status"},{"type":"text","value":": Current status ('disabled' | 'exceeded' | 'idle')"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getRemainingInWindow()"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getMsUntilNextWindow()"},{"type":"text","value":" for current window capacity and timing."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tvalue","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TValue"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tselected","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TSelected"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":" = {\n}"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"value","children":[{"type":"text","value":"value"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"initialoptions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"initialOptions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/SolidPacerOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SolidPacerOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/SolidRateLimiterOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SolidRateLimiterOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Setter"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"},{"type":"text","value":">, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":">>"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"selector","children":[{"type":"text","value":"selector?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state"},{"type":"text","value":") => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"["},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Accessor"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"},{"type":"text","value":">, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Setter"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"},{"type":"text","value":">, "},{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/SolidRateLimiter.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SolidRateLimiter"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Setter"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"},{"type":"text","value":">, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":">]"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Default behavior - no reactive state subscriptions\nconst [value, setValue, rateLimiter] = createRateLimitedSignal(0, {\n  limit: 5,\n  window: 60000,\n  windowType: 'sliding'\n});\n\n// Opt-in to reactive updates when limit state changes (optimized for UI feedback)\nconst [value, setValue, rateLimiter] = createRateLimitedSignal(\n  0,\n  { limit: 5, window: 60000 },\n  (state) => ({ isExceeded: state.isExceeded })\n);\n\n// With rejection callback and fixed window\nconst [value, setValue] = createRateLimitedSignal(0, {\n  limit: 3,\n  window: 5000,\n  windowType: 'fixed',\n  onReject: (rateLimiter) => {\n    alert(`Rate limit reached. Try again in ${rateLimiter.getMsUntilNextWindow()}ms`);\n  }\n});\n\n// Access rateLimiter state via signals\nconst handleSubmit = () => {\n  const remaining = rateLimiter.getRemainingInWindow();\n  if (remaining > 0) {\n    setValue(newValue);\n  } else {\n    showRateLimitWarning();\n  }\n};","lang":"tsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"state-management-and-selector","text":"State Management and Selector","level":2},{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tvalue","text":"TValue","level":3},{"id":"tselected","text":"TSelected","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"value","text":"value","level":3},{"id":"initialoptions","text":"initialOptions","level":3},{"id":"selector","text":"selector?","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction createRateLimitedSignal<TValue, TSelected>(\n   value,\n   initialOptions,\n   selector?): [Accessor<TValue>, Setter<TValue>, SolidRateLimiter<Setter<TValue>, TSelected>];\n```\n\nDefined in: [rate-limiter/createRateLimitedSignal.ts:97](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/solid-pacer/src/rate-limiter/createRateLimitedSignal.ts#L97)\n\nA Solid hook that creates a rate-limited state value that enforces a hard limit on state updates within a time window.\nThis hook combines Solid's createSignal with rate limiting functionality to provide controlled state updates.\n\nRate limiting is a simple \"hard limit\" approach - it allows all updates until the limit is reached, then blocks\nsubsequent updates until the window resets. Unlike throttling or debouncing, it does not attempt to space out\nor intelligently collapse updates. This can lead to bursts of rapid updates followed by periods of no updates.\n\nThe rate limiter supports two types of windows:\n- 'fixed': A strict window that resets after the window period. All updates within the window count\n  towards the limit, and the window resets completely after the period.\n- 'sliding': A rolling window that allows updates as old ones expire. This provides a more\n  consistent rate of updates over time.\n\nFor smoother update patterns, consider:\n- createThrottledSignal: When you want consistent spacing between updates (e.g. UI changes)\n- createDebouncedSignal: When you want to collapse rapid updates into a single update (e.g. search input)\n\nRate limiting should primarily be used when you need to enforce strict limits, like API rate limits.\n\nThe hook returns a tuple containing:\n- The rate-limited state value accessor\n- A rate-limited setter function that respects the configured limits\n- The rateLimiter instance for additional control\n\nFor more direct control over rate limiting without state management,\nconsider using the lower-level createRateLimiter hook instead.\n\n## State Management and Selector\n\nThe hook uses TanStack Store for reactive state management via the underlying rate limiter instance.\nThe `selector` parameter allows you to specify which rate limiter state changes will trigger reactive updates,\noptimizing performance by preventing unnecessary subscriptions when irrelevant state changes occur.\n\n**By default, there will be no reactive state subscriptions** and you must opt-in to state\ntracking by providing a selector function. This prevents unnecessary reactive updates and gives you\nfull control over when your component subscribes to state changes. Only when you provide a selector will\nthe reactive system track the selected state values.\n\nAvailable rate limiter state properties:\n- `executionCount`: Number of function executions\n- `executionTimes`: Timestamps of executions tracked for the current window\n- `maybeExecuteCount`: Number of calls to maybeExecute\n- `rejectionCount`: Number of calls rejected by the rate limit\n- `isExceeded`: Whether the rate limit has been reached\n- `status`: Current status ('disabled' | 'exceeded' | 'idle')\n\nUse `getRemainingInWindow()` and `getMsUntilNextWindow()` for current window capacity and timing.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TValue\n\n`TValue`\n\n### TSelected\n\n`TSelected` = \\{\n\\}\n\n## Parameters\n\n### value\n\n`TValue`\n\n### initialOptions\n\n[`SolidPacerOptions`](../type-aliases/SolidPacerOptions.md)\\<[`SolidRateLimiterOptions`](../interfaces/SolidRateLimiterOptions.md)\\<`Setter`\\<`TValue`\\>, `TSelected`\\>\\>\n\n### selector?\n\n(`state`) => `TSelected`\n\n## Returns\n\n\\[`Accessor`\\<`TValue`\\>, `Setter`\\<`TValue`\\>, [`SolidRateLimiter`](../interfaces/SolidRateLimiter.md)\\<`Setter`\\<`TValue`\\>, `TSelected`\\>\\]\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\n// Default behavior - no reactive state subscriptions\nconst [value, setValue, rateLimiter] = createRateLimitedSignal(0, {\n  limit: 5,\n  window: 60000,\n  windowType: 'sliding'\n});\n\n// Opt-in to reactive updates when limit state changes (optimized for UI feedback)\nconst [value, setValue, rateLimiter] = createRateLimitedSignal(\n  0,\n  { limit: 5, window: 60000 },\n  (state) => ({ isExceeded: state.isExceeded })\n);\n\n// With rejection callback and fixed window\nconst [value, setValue] = createRateLimitedSignal(0, {\n  limit: 3,\n  window: 5000,\n  windowType: 'fixed',\n  onReject: (rateLimiter) => {\n    alert(`Rate limit reached. Try again in ${rateLimiter.getMsUntilNextWindow()}ms`);\n  }\n});\n\n// Access rateLimiter state via signals\nconst handleSubmit = () => {\n  const remaining = rateLimiter.getRemainingInWindow();\n  if (remaining > 0) {\n    setValue(newValue);\n  } else {\n    showRateLimitWarning();\n  }\n};\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: createRateLimitedSignal\ntitle: createRateLimitedSignal\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction createRateLimitedSignal<TValue, TSelected>(\n   value,\n   initialOptions,\n   selector?): [Accessor<TValue>, Setter<TValue>, SolidRateLimiter<Setter<TValue>, TSelected>];\n```\n\nDefined in: [rate-limiter/createRateLimitedSignal.ts:97](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/solid-pacer/src/rate-limiter/createRateLimitedSignal.ts#L97)\n\nA Solid hook that creates a rate-limited state value that enforces a hard limit on state updates within a time window.\nThis hook combines Solid's createSignal with rate limiting functionality to provide controlled state updates.\n\nRate limiting is a simple \"hard limit\" approach - it allows all updates until the limit is reached, then blocks\nsubsequent updates until the window resets. Unlike throttling or debouncing, it does not attempt to space out\nor intelligently collapse updates. This can lead to bursts of rapid updates followed by periods of no updates.\n\nThe rate limiter supports two types of windows:\n- 'fixed': A strict window that resets after the window period. All updates within the window count\n  towards the limit, and the window resets completely after the period.\n- 'sliding': A rolling window that allows updates as old ones expire. This provides a more\n  consistent rate of updates over time.\n\nFor smoother update patterns, consider:\n- createThrottledSignal: When you want consistent spacing between updates (e.g. UI changes)\n- createDebouncedSignal: When you want to collapse rapid updates into a single update (e.g. search input)\n\nRate limiting should primarily be used when you need to enforce strict limits, like API rate limits.\n\nThe hook returns a tuple containing:\n- The rate-limited state value accessor\n- A rate-limited setter function that respects the configured limits\n- The rateLimiter instance for additional control\n\nFor more direct control over rate limiting without state management,\nconsider using the lower-level createRateLimiter hook instead.\n\n## State Management and Selector\n\nThe hook uses TanStack Store for reactive state management via the underlying rate limiter instance.\nThe `selector` parameter allows you to specify which rate limiter state changes will trigger reactive updates,\noptimizing performance by preventing unnecessary subscriptions when irrelevant state changes occur.\n\n**By default, there will be no reactive state subscriptions** and you must opt-in to state\ntracking by providing a selector function. This prevents unnecessary reactive updates and gives you\nfull control over when your component subscribes to state changes. Only when you provide a selector will\nthe reactive system track the selected state values.\n\nAvailable rate limiter state properties:\n- `executionCount`: Number of function executions\n- `executionTimes`: Timestamps of executions tracked for the current window\n- `maybeExecuteCount`: Number of calls to maybeExecute\n- `rejectionCount`: Number of calls rejected by the rate limit\n- `isExceeded`: Whether the rate limit has been reached\n- `status`: Current status ('disabled' | 'exceeded' | 'idle')\n\nUse `getRemainingInWindow()` and `getMsUntilNextWindow()` for current window capacity and timing.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TValue\n\n`TValue`\n\n### TSelected\n\n`TSelected` = \\{\n\\}\n\n## Parameters\n\n### value\n\n`TValue`\n\n### initialOptions\n\n[`SolidPacerOptions`](../type-aliases/SolidPacerOptions.md)\\<[`SolidRateLimiterOptions`](../interfaces/SolidRateLimiterOptions.md)\\<`Setter`\\<`TValue`\\>, `TSelected`\\>\\>\n\n### selector?\n\n(`state`) => `TSelected`\n\n## Returns\n\n\\[`Accessor`\\<`TValue`\\>, `Setter`\\<`TValue`\\>, [`SolidRateLimiter`](../interfaces/SolidRateLimiter.md)\\<`Setter`\\<`TValue`\\>, `TSelected`\\>\\]\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\n// Default behavior - no reactive state subscriptions\nconst [value, setValue, rateLimiter] = createRateLimitedSignal(0, {\n  limit: 5,\n  window: 60000,\n  windowType: 'sliding'\n});\n\n// Opt-in to reactive updates when limit state changes (optimized for UI feedback)\nconst [value, setValue, rateLimiter] = createRateLimitedSignal(\n  0,\n  { limit: 5, window: 60000 },\n  (state) => ({ isExceeded: state.isExceeded })\n);\n\n// With rejection callback and fixed window\nconst [value, setValue] = createRateLimitedSignal(0, {\n  limit: 3,\n  window: 5000,\n  windowType: 'fixed',\n  onReject: (rateLimiter) => {\n    alert(`Rate limit reached. Try again in ${rateLimiter.getMsUntilNextWindow()}ms`);\n  }\n});\n\n// Access rateLimiter state via signals\nconst handleSubmit = () => {\n  const remaining = rateLimiter.getRemainingInWindow();\n  if (remaining > 0) {\n    setValue(newValue);\n  } else {\n    showRateLimitWarning();\n  }\n};\n```\n"}
